-- title:
--   Prolongation of p-torsion realised by a finite flat Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $p$ prime, $p \nmid N_0$ and $p \neq 2$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mathtt{LiesOverPrime}\ p$, i.e. $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying `IsJacobian` (the bundle of abelian-scheme, commutativity, additivity, Galois-equivariance, reduction and Hecke-equivariance conditions on $\Lambda$), let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data and let $F$ be a `NeronExtension` of $O$. Two inertia hypotheses are assumed: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) and every $m$-torsion point $x$ of $J_0(N_0p) = \mathtt{JZero}(N_0 p)$ one has $\sigma \cdot x - x \in O.\mathtt{toricPts}\ m$, the subgroup generated by the range of $O.\mathtt{toricPoint}\ m$; and for every $m > 0$ and such $\sigma, x$ one has $\sigma \cdot x - x \in O.\mathtt{finPts}\ m$, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion points whose associated point extends to a place over $\Lambda.\sigma_A$. Let $V$ be an additive subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ contained in the $p$-torsion, and let $H$ be a commutative ring which is a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathtt{ratLocalizedAt}\ p$, the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of fractions with denominator coprime to $p$. Assume given a bijection $e$ from `WithConv` applied to the type of $\mathtt{ratLocalizedAt}\ p$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a type carrying a multiplication) onto $V$, such that $e(f\cdot g) = e(f) + e(g)$, and such that whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$ pointwise on $H$ for a field automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, one has $e(g) = \sigma \cdot e(f)$ in $J_0(N_0p)$. The conclusion is that every $x \in V$ satisfies $F.\mathtt{ExtN}\ x$: there is a section $s$ of $F.g_N$ over $\mathtt{shPt}\ A$ with $(F.\mathtt{ptsN}\ x).1 = \mathtt{barPt}\ A$ followed by $s$, i.e. the point $x$ of the generic fibre extends to a point of the Néron extension over $A$.
--
--   This is the prolongation step in Raynaud's style: a subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)[p]$ which is realised, Galois-compatibly, as the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a finite flat commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ consists of points that extend over the valuation ring $A$. It is the content of the level-lowering bookkeeping lemma `le_finPts_of_hopf_of_forall_smul_sub_mem`, which packages the conclusion as an inclusion of $V$ into the finite part of the Néron extension.
-- source:
